WEBVTT

00:01.030 --> 00:04.000
What the heck's going on in my head?

00:05.000 --> 00:06.330
Hey, Zed...

00:06.330 --> 00:08.040
Could you tell me something?

00:08.040 --> 00:10.910
What's with you breaking all
these doors and gates?

00:10.910 --> 00:12.570
You see...

00:12.570 --> 00:16.200
I've got this feeling that if I break doors,
I can go somewhere.

00:16.710 --> 00:18.150
Have you remembered something?!

00:18.150 --> 00:20.050
You did, didn't you, Mom?

00:20.050 --> 00:22.020
Is there something about white feathers?

00:46.810 --> 00:54.550
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

00:54.550 --> 01:01.510
Tooku tooi basho e to

01:14.870 --> 01:21.080
Kaze ni fukare aruite yuku

01:21.080 --> 01:28.040
Umarekita imi o shiritakute

01:28.250 --> 01:34.560
Tatoeba ushinau toki ga kitemo

01:34.560 --> 01:41.690
Dakishimeru koto ima, erabou

01:44.130 --> 01:51.540
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

01:51.540 --> 01:57.510
Nakusenai mono ni mukatte

01:57.510 --> 02:05.150
Kagayaita yume dake o taguriyosenagara

02:05.150 --> 02:12.030
Tooku tooi basho e to

02:36.420 --> 02:40.560
Episode 2
A New World

02:38.390 --> 02:40.560


Where am I?

02:40.560 --> 02:41.350
Where am I?

02:42.090 --> 02:44.060
The wind!

02:44.060 --> 02:46.190
The wind is blowing...

02:47.800 --> 02:49.590
Who the hell is he?

02:51.730 --> 02:53.530
Go on, Zuigyu!

02:55.500 --> 02:57.130
Master Zico!

03:21.860 --> 03:23.830
What the hell is this place?!

03:29.940 --> 03:31.440
I leave the boy to you.

03:31.440 --> 03:33.070
Master!

03:43.120 --> 03:44.740
Zegyu!

03:49.790 --> 03:53.090
Fyron, finish him off now!

04:09.640 --> 04:12.680
I would say that ends our match.

04:12.680 --> 04:14.650
Damn it...

04:15.650 --> 04:18.780
Who the hell are these people?

04:37.140 --> 04:40.340
I will be taking your spirit.

04:40.340 --> 04:42.140
Master Zico!

04:42.140 --> 04:44.110
Look at his left hand!

05:04.170 --> 05:06.290
That was one weird dream.

05:07.000 --> 05:10.630
You're having bad dreams from
sleeping in places like that.

05:10.840 --> 05:13.680
Noah, your body!

05:13.680 --> 05:15.880
Right, don't worry about it.

05:15.880 --> 05:17.670
This happens all the time.

05:19.050 --> 05:20.340
Noah!

05:26.620 --> 05:29.590
It's okay, this happens all the time.

05:30.120 --> 05:31.750
Don't worry about it.

05:32.090 --> 05:33.720
Noah...

05:34.160 --> 05:38.960
Anyhow, do you think I could come here again?

05:40.130 --> 05:44.310
My name's Noah, Noah Voilier.

05:44.310 --> 05:46.100
Nice to meet you.

05:47.740 --> 05:49.410
What's your name?

05:49.410 --> 05:51.180
Me? I'm...

05:51.180 --> 05:53.480
You're a shard caster.

05:54.320 --> 05:57.450
But before you become a nuisance...

05:57.450 --> 05:59.080
I'll kill you!

06:05.560 --> 06:07.190
Mom!

06:07.760 --> 06:09.800
C'mon, tell me!

06:09.800 --> 06:12.600
What the heck is a shard caster?!

06:13.100 --> 06:14.730
Mom!

06:25.210 --> 06:26.840
Noah!

06:32.490 --> 06:34.280
Noah!

06:41.900 --> 06:44.190
So, it was for real.

06:44.800 --> 06:45.970
Noah...

06:45.970 --> 06:47.940
Hey, are you all right?

06:50.410 --> 06:52.030
Who are you?!

06:53.140 --> 06:55.140
Me? I'm Roya.

06:55.140 --> 06:57.450
This is Master Zico, the Elder.

06:57.450 --> 06:59.410
He's my teacher.

07:00.150 --> 07:01.150
Teacher?

07:01.150 --> 07:02.150
Who are you?

07:02.150 --> 07:04.950
Me? Zed...

07:05.650 --> 07:07.120
Zed?

07:07.120 --> 07:09.120
Well, I've never seen anyone
dressed like that before.

07:09.120 --> 07:10.660
Where'd you come from?

07:10.660 --> 07:11.660
Calm.

07:11.660 --> 07:14.960
Calm? Never heard of the place.

07:14.960 --> 07:17.000
Where are we?

07:17.000 --> 07:18.600
This is Templar.

07:18.600 --> 07:20.230
Templar?

07:20.700 --> 07:22.830
I've never heard of such a place...

07:30.180 --> 07:32.280
That's the castle's windmill.

07:32.280 --> 07:35.250
Whoa, hey! Where are you going?

07:37.120 --> 07:38.990
What a weird kid...

07:38.990 --> 07:41.280
What could he have come here for?

08:20.290 --> 08:21.920
Hey, you!

08:22.360 --> 08:24.490
Haven't seen that kind of outfit before.

08:24.970 --> 08:26.760
So, where are you from?

08:27.500 --> 08:28.640
Calm.

08:28.640 --> 08:31.310
Calm? Where the heck's that?

08:31.310 --> 08:32.710
What a weirdo...

08:32.710 --> 08:34.040
Here, come with me.

08:34.040 --> 08:35.670
What's your problem?

08:35.880 --> 08:37.380
Resist me, will you?!

08:37.380 --> 08:39.010
Get him!

08:41.750 --> 08:43.550
Why, you little...

08:50.630 --> 08:51.630
Master Zico!

08:51.630 --> 08:54.430
We've caused quite a disturbance.

08:54.430 --> 08:56.330
Not at all, sir!

08:56.330 --> 08:59.300
Does this mean he's your pupil, sir?

08:59.570 --> 09:01.870
Something like that, I suppose.

09:09.440 --> 09:11.310
Master Zico...

09:11.310 --> 09:14.250
Why are we taking him to Master Sebastian?

09:14.250 --> 09:18.590
Why? Oh, well, because we can't have this
boy causing any more disturbances.

09:18.590 --> 09:23.220
I thought maybe Sebastian could
give him good counsel.

09:32.170 --> 09:34.800
It appears that you have somehow crossed over

09:34.800 --> 09:38.260
to our space and time from a different dimension.

09:38.670 --> 09:40.810
Different dimension?

09:40.810 --> 09:44.710
You have come here by shifting from
a plane other than ours.

09:44.710 --> 09:46.050
Shifting?

09:46.050 --> 09:48.350
Dimensional teleportation, in other words.

09:48.980 --> 09:54.110
In theory, shifting should be a capability
limited to shard casters.

09:54.520 --> 09:56.290
Shard casters?

09:56.290 --> 09:58.920
Then, am I also a shard caster?

10:01.500 --> 10:06.530
Templar is wonderful country, which respects
the ideals of freedom and peace.

10:06.530 --> 10:12.000
We shard casters have a duty to serve as
this country's foremost protectors.

10:13.040 --> 10:15.840
Shard caster...

10:16.340 --> 10:18.310
How could I be one?

10:49.210 --> 10:51.840
Ah, nice spirit.

11:02.890 --> 11:04.360
The wind!

11:04.360 --> 11:07.660
So, how is the boy doing?

11:08.730 --> 11:10.360
Wait!

11:11.070 --> 11:12.400
Take it with you.

11:12.400 --> 11:16.200
You may go wherever the wind blows you,

11:16.200 --> 11:19.170
but you cannot defy fate.

11:19.570 --> 11:23.370
Place this atop your left hand.

11:33.190 --> 11:37.730
Boy, if you are destined to be a shard caster,

11:37.730 --> 11:40.850
then you will soon have need
of what I've given you.

11:41.600 --> 11:45.400
Sense your inner self, realize your fate,

11:45.400 --> 11:48.860
then carve your own path.

11:50.670 --> 11:53.440
I sense danger.

11:53.440 --> 11:55.840
I hope he'll be all right.

11:55.840 --> 11:59.300
You're as much a worrywart as ever.

12:00.080 --> 12:02.450
We can't just let him go like this, can we?

12:02.450 --> 12:04.920
I'll see to it that Dumas keeps watch on him.

12:07.560 --> 12:11.290
The wind cannot blow eternally;

12:11.290 --> 12:14.060
there will surely come a time when it stops.

12:14.060 --> 12:19.020
When that time comes, what will you do, boy?

12:34.920 --> 12:38.020
Fate? Shard caster?

12:38.020 --> 12:39.690
What's that supposed to mean?

12:39.690 --> 12:41.660
What are you doing up there?

12:42.360 --> 12:44.290
I haven't seen you before.

12:44.290 --> 12:45.920
Looks mighty suspicious to me.

12:46.530 --> 12:48.150
Get down here now!

12:48.930 --> 12:51.060
Hey! Get back here!

12:53.730 --> 12:54.440
He's over there!

12:54.440 --> 12:55.740
Don't let him get away!
He's over there!

12:55.740 --> 12:57.360
Head him off!

13:09.550 --> 13:11.620
That's a Templan sword!

13:11.620 --> 13:13.420
Where did you get hold of that?!

13:36.080 --> 13:38.040
There he is! This way!

14:05.040 --> 14:07.010
A spirit!

14:07.340 --> 14:09.310
Spirit?

14:21.260 --> 14:23.090
What's going on?!

14:23.090 --> 14:24.720
This way!

14:25.960 --> 14:28.090
Come with me, quick!

14:29.600 --> 14:31.220
She's...

14:36.900 --> 14:38.870
After them! Don't let them get away!

14:40.370 --> 14:42.340
This way, hurry!

14:43.380 --> 14:46.010
Are you a shard caster?

14:47.310 --> 14:48.380
That's right.

14:48.380 --> 14:51.010
Which means that old guy...

14:52.050 --> 14:55.020
For now, let's just get you somewhere safe.

14:55.790 --> 14:57.420
Follow me.

14:58.160 --> 14:59.790
This way.

15:05.700 --> 15:08.500
If we can get across that bridge,
we'll lose those soldiers.

15:14.040 --> 15:15.110
Mr. Dumas?!

15:15.110 --> 15:16.280
Dumas?

15:16.280 --> 15:18.350
He's the shard champion of Templar,

15:18.350 --> 15:20.310
not anyone we can handle!

15:22.350 --> 15:24.320
Then he's the strongest, huh?

15:25.290 --> 15:28.410
Don't think you'll escape so easily after your
senseless and wanton rampage.

15:29.920 --> 15:30.930
C'mon.

15:30.930 --> 15:32.530
I haven't done a thing.

15:32.530 --> 15:35.500
You guys started this ruckus all on your own!

15:51.750 --> 15:53.780
The shard champion, huh?

15:53.780 --> 15:55.410
Damn!

15:58.290 --> 16:00.750
What do you intend to do, Zico?

16:00.750 --> 16:05.380
He strikes me as a guy who's only
going to stir up trouble.

16:08.730 --> 16:11.830
It's exactly as I had thought!

16:11.830 --> 16:14.030
The charges will be dropped soon enough.

16:14.030 --> 16:15.700
After all, we're witnesses.

16:15.700 --> 16:16.300
However!
After all, we're witnesses.

16:16.300 --> 16:17.040
However!
All that's left is to turn on the charm.

16:17.040 --> 16:18.270
All that's left is to turn on the charm.

16:18.610 --> 16:20.470
You're awake, boy?

16:20.470 --> 16:21.980
Where'd she go?

16:21.980 --> 16:25.310
If you mean Roya, she's in another cell.

16:25.310 --> 16:26.310
Why?

16:26.310 --> 16:28.620
For helping you to escape.

16:28.620 --> 16:31.720
I never did anything wrong,
and she's totally innocent!

16:31.720 --> 16:33.420
We know that,

16:33.420 --> 16:37.050
but this is just until the charges are dropped.

16:38.960 --> 16:40.930
But she's innocent...

16:45.300 --> 16:47.100
Where's her cell?

17:05.190 --> 17:06.810
Who's there?

17:08.390 --> 17:09.390
It's me.

17:09.390 --> 17:11.460
Zed! How?

17:11.460 --> 17:13.030
Why did you...

17:13.030 --> 17:14.760
What are you here for?

17:14.760 --> 17:16.400
Stop your yapping.

17:16.400 --> 17:18.020
Just come on, will you?

17:20.070 --> 17:21.860
What's his problem!

17:26.570 --> 17:27.780
They've broken out!

17:27.780 --> 17:28.380
After them!

17:28.380 --> 17:29.110
Don't let them get away!
After them!

17:29.110 --> 17:29.840
Don't let them get away!
There they are!

17:29.840 --> 17:31.140
Move!
There they are!

17:36.980 --> 17:39.780
Damn! Cut off both ways.

17:40.650 --> 17:42.450
What should we do?

17:44.760 --> 17:47.030
A spirit! They're going to get away!

17:47.030 --> 17:48.820
After them! Hurry!

17:50.600 --> 17:52.390
There it is!

17:53.970 --> 17:56.940
What a gorgeous spirit!

17:58.270 --> 18:00.070
They took off!

18:00.070 --> 18:01.710
Hurry!

18:01.710 --> 18:03.340
Don't let them escape!

18:05.210 --> 18:07.510
This thing is a spirit?

18:07.510 --> 18:11.790
That's right, it's my spirit, Apcarel.

18:11.790 --> 18:15.790
Do all shard casters have spirits?

18:15.790 --> 18:17.560
Not necessarily.

18:17.560 --> 18:22.520
Those who can command spirits are special,
even among shard casters.

18:23.560 --> 18:27.500
The more elite shard casters
have stronger spirits.

18:27.500 --> 18:30.640
But in order to control strong spirits,

18:30.640 --> 18:34.940
the shard caster must also become
sufficiently strong.

18:43.020 --> 18:46.140
Was that thing a spirit too?

18:57.400 --> 18:59.370
What a magnificent spirit!

19:00.000 --> 19:01.630
Who's there?!

19:02.140 --> 19:04.770
I've no name worth mentioning.

19:04.770 --> 19:09.400
I just want that spirit.

19:09.810 --> 19:11.910
Those tattoos around his eyes...

19:11.910 --> 19:13.250
He's a Zymotan soldier!

19:13.250 --> 19:15.220
Hand it over to me now,

19:15.220 --> 19:18.010
and we can avoid any unnecessary loss of life.

19:19.420 --> 19:21.550
Looks like I got to kill you then, huh?

19:46.280 --> 19:47.910
Go!

19:53.450 --> 19:55.080
Apcarel!

20:01.400 --> 20:03.020
Zed!

20:04.000 --> 20:08.800
If I kill you, that spirit will be mine!

20:22.380 --> 20:26.010
Has the wind stopped?

20:28.960 --> 20:34.090
Tell me, who are you?!

21:59.150 --> 22:01.110
Did you see that, Zico?

22:06.690 --> 22:11.150
Come on, tell me.

22:12.290 --> 22:19.260
Are you my spirit?

22:20.200 --> 22:23.670
Who the heck are...

22:23.670 --> 22:26.640
Whoa, hang on! Hey!

22:27.010 --> 22:28.310
Zed!

22:28.310 --> 22:29.940
Zed!

22:50.460 --> 22:54.330
Kimi no sono kokoro no naka o nozoite
shiritai sono kimochi to hyoujou

22:54.330 --> 22:58.240
Hitori seotta kimi no sugata kirari
hikaru namida no wake wa

22:58.240 --> 23:01.810
Kikazu ni iwazu ni okuru yo eeru
sagashiteru kotae no aida ni

23:01.810 --> 23:05.940
Kodawarisugizu kangaesugizu asu
no kimi ni komorebi kanjiru

23:07.650 --> 23:09.480
Very very much de ii kanji

23:09.480 --> 23:11.280
Very very good kimi to boku

23:11.280 --> 23:15.160
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai to omotterun da

23:15.160 --> 23:16.990
Very very much itsudatte

23:16.990 --> 23:18.830
Very very good kawaranai

23:18.830 --> 23:24.790
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

23:30.300 --> 23:32.770
Mayoi no naka kono yasashisa kanji

23:34.070 --> 23:36.540
Donna toki mo kimi o zutto shinji

23:37.810 --> 23:41.720
Koko ni ookiku hirogaru keshiki
buruusukai no hi no shita de

23:41.720 --> 23:45.850
li kibun ii mibun ii jibun zutto koko ni itai kibun

23:47.320 --> 23:49.120
Very very much de ii kanji

23:49.120 --> 23:50.960
Very very good kimi to boku

23:50.960 --> 23:54.760
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai toomotterun da

23:54.760 --> 23:56.630
Very very much itsudatte

23:56.630 --> 23:58.500
Very very good kawaranai

23:58.500 --> 24:04.460
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

24:16.780 --> 24:19.950
Next time, "Those With Power"

24:17.250 --> 24:19.950
Next Time
Those With Power
